<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4007] SQL: QueryMetrics.minimumTime() is always zero.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4007</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt; QueryMetrics.minimumTime() is always zero, because internal AtomicInteger initialized with zero and code that change minTime looks like&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;minTime.setIfLess(duration);&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Obviously that execution time is always &amp;gt;=0 and any number is always is greate than zero and metrics never updated.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
